  userData: "Created with built-in image_gen. Rebirth screenshot reference: https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=350608638. Final prompt: Game UI asset: blank death diary paper from The Binding of Isaac: Rebirth (2014). Draw the simple pale grey-ivory paper exactly in the pixel-art language of that game: vertical near-rectangle, width/height ratio 0.87, slight irregular wavy outline and a few shallow notches, thin 1-2 pixel muted brown-grey outline, one tiny dog-eared fold at bottom-left, a few VERY PALE sparse angular crease shapes near the edges. Low resolution game sprite roughly 200x230 pixels enlarged with hard nearest-neighbor pixels and a tiny flat palette. The ENTIRE page interior is FILLED COMPLETELY SOLID with pale ivory #e7e3d1. Completely blank central field. No text, no doodles, no grain, no stains, no central shadow, no vignette, no gradients, no holes, no dark interior regions. The page is perfectly upright; do not tilt it. Important technical asset background: OUTSIDE the paper is perfectly uniform opaque NEON MAGENTA #ff00ff. Do not use transparency anywhere. The neon magenta exists ONLY outside the page, NEVER inside. Paper and outline fully opaque. Canvas portrait approx 1024x1184, page filling 96% of canvas. No cast shadow or other object. Final PNG export has real alpha outside the paper. Only the edge-connected magenta exterior was removed; the paper interior and original GUID are preserved. The prefab uses the standard Unity UI material. Edge cleanup: residual magenta-contaminated contour pixels within 8 px of transparency were replaced with the nearest untainted contour palette color. Interior paper colors and alpha silhouette retained."
